* **A tiny right‑push (action = 2) when the velocity is still very low on the right side** – this gives the car the extra momentum needed to cross the summit.

These observations confirm the core intuition of the earlier rules, but they also highlight that the **thresholds (0.02 m/s, 0.019 m/s, etc.) are too low** for the steep part of the right hill.

