|`‑0.2 ≤ position < 0.0`|Prevent “stall” at the centre|If the car is still moving left (`velocity < 0`) we immediately push right; otherwise we coast to keep the already‑gained rightward speed.|
|`‑0.5 ≤ position < ‑0.2`|Escape the left dip quickly|When the car is still sliding left we give a *full left* thrust (`action = 0`) to climb out of the left valley; once it has a rightward drift we switch to right thrust.|
|`position < ‑0.5`|Never stay idle in the far left|A hard left push drives the car toward the centre of the valley, where the subsequent rules take over.|

