### 2️⃣  Updated “Bang‑Bang’’ Strategy  

Below is a clean, comment‑rich version that you can copy straight into your controller.  It is deliberately **simple** (only a handful of thresholds) yet captures the three‑phase intuition:

```python
# --------------------------------------------------------------
#   MountainCar “Bang‑Bang’’ controller
#   0 = accelerate left   (push downhill to the left)
#   1 = no acceleration   (coast)
#   2 = accelerate right  (push uphill to the right)
# --------------------------------------------------------------

def choose_action(position, velocity):
    # 1️⃣  Goal reached – stay idle
    if position >= 0.5:
        return 1                       # we are done, no more thrust

    # 2️⃣  Very far left – we must build momentum by pushing left
    #    The classic optimal policy pushes left until x ≈ -0.55
    if position < -0.55:
        return 0                       # hard left thrust

    # 3️⃣  Still moving left (negative velocity) – keep pushing left
    #    This guarantees that we will eventually cross the bottom
    if velocity < 0.0:
        return 0                       # keep accelerating left

    # 4️⃣  We are on the right side of the valley (position > -0.2)
    #    and already have a decent positive speed.
    #    When we are close to the goal and fast enough, we can coast.
    if position > 0.3 and velocity > 0.04:
        return 1                       # coast – avoid overshooting

    # 5️⃣  Default case – push right.
    #    This covers:
    #       * the bottom region (‑0.55 ≤ x < -0.2) once we have positive speed
    #       * the middle region (‑0.2 ≤ x < 0.3) where we still need thrust
    return 2
```

**Why each clause matters**

| Clause | Situation | Why this action? |
|--------|-----------|------------------|
| `position >= 0.5` | Goal reached | No more reward penalty, stay still |
| `position < -0.55` | Far left, low kinetic energy | The only way to gain *any* momentum is to push left (the car can’t climb the right hill from here) |
| `velocity < 0` | Still moving left even after we have crossed `‑0.55` | Continuing left thrust prevents the car from stalling at the bottom |
| `position > 0.3 and velocity > 0.04` | Near the right hill, already fast enough | Coasting saves the remaining time steps; an extra thrust would just waste a step and could even push the car back if it overshoots |
| `else` | All other states (bottom, middle, or modest right‑ward speed) | Push right – this is the “bang” that converts the stored kinetic energy into altitude |

