|--------|-----------|------------------|
| `position >= 0.5` | Goal reached | No more reward penalty, stay still |
| `position < -0.55` | Far left, low kinetic energy | The only way to gain *any* momentum is to push left (the car can’t climb the right hill from here) |
| `velocity < 0` | Still moving left even after we have crossed `‑0.55` | Continuing left thrust prevents the car from stalling at the bottom |
| `position > 0.3 and velocity > 0.04` | Near the right hill, already fast enough | Coasting saves the remaining time steps; an extra thrust would just waste a step and could even push the car back if it overshoots |
| `else` | All other states (bottom, middle, or modest right‑ward speed) | Push right – this is the “bang” that converts the stored kinetic energy into altitude |

