2. **No “momentum‑building” phase** – when the car is still on the left slope (≈ ‑0.3 … ‑0.45 m) the optimal behaviour is to *push left* until the velocity reaches a safe negative value (≈ ‑0.07 … ‑0.09 m/s). Our rule only fired when `velocity > -0.06`, which is already too high; the car never got the extra push it needed to roll down the left side.  

